    <briefdescription>
<para>Fully-async training job orchestration interface. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Design constraints:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1training_1_1_i_training_pipeline_1a29058bd270f7d1eb98c5b0b5dc6b5d55" kindref="member">submit()</ref> returns a future immediately; no blocking calls on the public API.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1training_1_1_i_training_pipeline_1a435b1cab126e3225c70f9d2a79f4f6f8" kindref="member">cancel()</ref> is best-effort; returns AlreadyCompleted if the job has finished.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1training_1_1_i_training_pipeline_1ab0194cce21035425095551c1e6df76c5" kindref="member">status()</ref> is safe to call from any thread.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1training_1_1_training_pipeline" kindref="compound">TrainingPipeline</ref> (concrete implementation) </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
